1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:17,934
EPISODE 5
HAPPY MOMENT

2
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:42,500
Hmm.

3
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:47,088
Ka-ze-haya!
Where do you think you're going, huh?

4
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,883
- I've already got your song loaded up.
- Sorry, but I--

5
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:52,802
But nothing.
You're not sneaking out of your own party!

6
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:54,345
- Hey, Kazehaya.
- Huh?

7
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:56,598
What time did you say
we had this room till?

8
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:59,768
- Nine.
- Oh, hey, there you are. For you.

9
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,436
Let's get an extension.

10
00:01:01,519 --> 00:01:05,607
- Or an after-party.
- Yo, Kazehaya. Over here. Look.

11
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:10,361
Sorry. Party's all yours from here on out.
Do what you want.

12
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,073
What the heck, dude.

13
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,908
- Where's he going?
- Kazehaya?

14
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:24,584
Huh?

15
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:28,588
Kazehaya.

16
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:30,965
Sorry.

17
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,967
- I'm okay now.
- Ah.

18
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:38,098
- Ha-ha! Hey, don't you worry, kid.
- Pin?!

19
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,390
Why are you here?

20
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:42,811
- Now, now. Don't sweat the details.
- Thank you for the tissue.

21
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:46,564
Just a little housekeeping
after a quarrel, that's all.

22
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,274
What quarrel?

23
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,276
Hey, Kuronuma.

24
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,321
- You should probably head back first.
- Huh?

25
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:56,032
Sure.

26
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:18,096
Been meanin' to ask ya.
How long have you two been goin' out?

27
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,431
That came outta nowhere!

28
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,767
I dunno, six months?

29
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,936
Six months, you say?

30
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:26,938
Impressive, young man.

31
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:28,731
Huh! Very impressive!

32
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,150
Wha-- what do you mean?

33
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,736
For six whole months, you've resisted
the temptations of the flesh.

34
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:35,405
Amazing!

35
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:37,991
A man of my experience
can tell just by looking.

36
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:39,826
Wha-- Tell what?

37
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:44,706
Listen. The path
which you have chosen is correct.

38
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:45,874
Excellent job.

39
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:48,793
Don't you ever change, kid.

40
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:53,715
Uh-- uh-- uh-- Wha-- Ne-- never?

41
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:54,799
Seriously, though.

42
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:59,387
You know what the right thing to do is,
don't you? And you're trying your best?

43
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:07,687
Yeah. I am trying, but I don't know
if it's actually the right thing.

44
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,524
- Well, that's too bad 'cause neither do I!
- What?

45
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:13,860
All right! I think it's about that time!

46
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:16,654
Get ready, kids,
I'm about to give you the boot!

47
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:22,952
It's that late?
What do we do? Where's Kazehaya?

48
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:25,121
He's not the only one missing.

49
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,041
Closing time, kiddos!

50
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:30,293
All right, I'm putting a bow
on this shindig!

51
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,046
Now, get your butts outta here,
it's past your bedtime!

52
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:34,339
Oh hush!

53
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,466
And don't you even
think about an after-party.

54
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:39,385
You kids better head
straight on home. No detours.

55
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:42,096
Come on, it's Christmas!
Can't you turn a blind eye?

56
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:46,059
Sorry, pal. My personal rule is
I only turn one blind eye a day.

57
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:48,102
And I've already met my quota.

58
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:51,898
Go on, beat it! Scram.

59
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:56,277
Hey, is that Ayane's bag?

60
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:00,031
Y-- yeah.

61
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,075
Master.

62
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:05,995
Ayane.

63
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:07,622
Sawako.

64
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:13,711
Kento... is gonna walk me home.

65
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:28,017
Looks like that's that.

66
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:30,812
- Hey!
- Huh?

67
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:34,816
- Is the party breaking up already?
- Chizu. Here. Your bag.

68
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:37,902
Oh, thanks. Sorry to trouble you.

69
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:39,821
Huh? Where's Yano-chin?

70
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:41,656
Um, she just left.

71
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:43,533
What?! Just like that?

72
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:48,955
Hey, she's not angry at me
for suddenly disappearing, is she?

73
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:51,791
- Oh no, she's not mad at all.
- Chizuru.

74
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:52,792
Ready to go?

75
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:54,877
Uh, yeah. Coming.

76
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:00,133
Sawa.

77
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,594
Hey, uh, let's find time to talk later.

78
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:06,389
Mm!

79
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:18,192
I'll give her the present on the way home.

80
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:22,530
I have no idea
if it's the right thing or not.

81
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:25,491
I just...

82
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,830
Whenever I get too close, I lose control.

83
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:37,086
If Kuronuma were within my reach
and I held out my hand... and touched her,

84
00:05:38,296 --> 00:05:42,967
I know for a fact I'd pull her in
and hold her as tight as I could.

85
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:45,303
I would kiss her.

86
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:49,140
All the distance
between us would fade away.

87
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:51,809
But that would be wrong.

88
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:55,188
What I really want is to cherish her.

89
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,731
Forever.

90
00:05:57,315 --> 00:06:00,568
And that means,
keeping a respectful distance.

91
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,363
You've been holdin' back, right?

92
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:13,456
You ready?

93
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,251
Mm... mmm.

94
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:20,046
Oh, it's those two.

95
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:22,173
Wait, are they still goin' out?

96
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:24,509
Man, I thought for sure
they had broken up.

97
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,094
They came to the party though.

98
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:29,430
Oh right.
You're not in our class, are you?

99
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:32,433
Let's go.

100
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,268
Yeah.

101
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:48,866
Man, I thought for sure
they had broken up.

102
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:02,463
Are we still... going out?

103
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:06,717
Can you blame me?
Kazehaya never tells me a thing.

104
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:17,770
Tomorrow is the start
of winter vacation... Kazehaya.

105
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:25,194
Maybe... this is what it's come to.

106
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:33,619
Maybe... one day...
we're both going to look up and realize

107
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:36,622
that we aren't a couple any longer.

108
00:07:38,624 --> 00:07:42,462
I've always dreaded
our time as a couple ending abruptly.

109
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,510
But, what if we're already...

110
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:51,929
What if

111
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:54,015
we're not...

112
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:58,019
So, yeah, things may be
a little weird between you at the moment.

113
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:00,521
But, if you close your eyes
and wait for five seconds,

114
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:03,441
well, I bet anything
things'll get sorted out.

115
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:19,290
Uh...

116
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:35,640
Wha--

117
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:37,099
Uh...

118
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:40,853
What's the matter, Kuronuma?

119
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:55,159
That's the last time...
I roll the dice.

120
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,959
You lied... to me.

121
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:10,967
Kazehaya, you lied. You're a liar!

122
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:16,556
You said you wouldn't know
what to do if I did that again. You liar.

123
00:09:17,056 --> 00:09:21,435
You say nothing's bothering you,
but I know that's not true.

124
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:26,357
All I wanted for us today...

125
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:29,569
...was to be able to spend time together.

126
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:34,073
Last year, I desperately wanted us
to have this time.

127
00:09:35,616 --> 00:09:39,370
I understand that you've been
really busy with your work...

128
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,247
I get it, I do.

129
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,500
The present I wanted him
to accept from me...

130
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,463
I can't give it,
even though we're together now.

131
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:54,844
But......I feel lonelier
than when I was by myself.

132
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:04,145
Is being with me
what's been bothering you?

133
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:06,314
Did you start having second thoughts?

134
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,898
Do you...

135
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:12,320
not like me anymore?

136
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:17,533
You don't like me as I am anymore?

137
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:22,496
Of course he doesn't. Why would he?

138
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:34,443
I like you.

139
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,195
I like you.

140
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:39,323
I like you!

141
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:54,296
Kazehaya.

142
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,300
Kazehaya!

143
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:45,181
Finally.

144
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:49,185
You're finally... looking at me.

145
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,741
Yeah, 'cause I really love you.

146
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:12,082
Yeah.

147
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:23,260
This is what really mattered.

148
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:41,779
I wanna talk. But properly.

149
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:45,282
It might take a while though.

150
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,955
I'd like that too.

151
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,380
Oh, yes, hi, Mom.

152
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:04,218
Yeah, I'm fine.
I, uh... I might be out a while.

153
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:08,055
Right. Yes. He's with me.

154
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:09,557
Huh? Dad?

155
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,141
Uh.

156
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:15,062
No, wait, Dad. Hang on. Just this once!

157
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:17,314
After that, I'll... I'll do better.

158
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,817
I swear, I'll double down
on my chores and studies.

159
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,026
Kuronuma.

160
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:24,071
Is it okay if I talk to him a sec?

161
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:31,036
Uh, hello? This is Kazehaya. I, uh...

162
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:34,415
Just one hour.
That's all I'm asking for, sir.

163
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:35,833
Yes.

164
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:39,128
I'll make sure
she gets home safe. Yes, sir.

165
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:40,588
Yes.

166
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:42,131
Right.

167
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:53,934
I will. Thank you, sir.

168
00:14:54,768 --> 00:14:55,769
Goodbye.

169
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,108
Forty-five minutes, he said.

170
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:06,614
I tried, but that's all
he was willing to give me.

171
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,915
You see, Sawako, your dad understands.

172
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:18,918
He says that you've been brave
for long enough.

173
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:19,835
Huh?

174
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:48,155
Please, enjoy.

175
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:54,119
Last Christmas...
you couldn't make it, right?

176
00:15:55,829 --> 00:15:58,916
I swore that I'd never
let you feel sad or alone.

177
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,127
I told myself I'd never let that happen.

178
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:06,298
That's when he...

179
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:08,509
But...

180
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:11,261
...in spite of that,
I'm the one who made you sad.

181
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:13,180
Sorry.

182
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:26,610
I kept thinking in circles,
and it made you anxious.

183
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:30,698
I'm sorry for that.
It wasn't my intention at all.

184
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:36,745
When I went over to your house
and met both your mother and father,

185
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:39,873
I, uh, I wanted to show how serious I was.

186
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:42,876
Show how I cherish you.

187
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:47,006
At least... that's what I wanted.

188
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:51,510
I'll treasure you
from now till the end of time.

189
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:53,721
My intentions for us are serious.

190
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:58,475
And as for Christmas,
after what happened last year,

191
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:02,396
I thought a group activity
would have made you happy.

192
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,859
Even so... there's another problem.

193
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:10,863
I don't have confidence.

194
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:14,116
Like that time on our class trip.

195
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:17,745
I lost my cool, immediately.

196
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:24,376
I don't know if you can
even imagine how much I like you.

197
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,383
It's true.

198
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:34,845
My imagination could never
fill in the blanks.

199
00:17:36,305 --> 00:17:40,059
From the very first day,
you weren't like anyone I'd ever met.

200
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:44,938
I mean it.

201
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:48,567
Ever since that time,
you've always been right here.

202
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:53,739
My heart has never been without you.

203
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:57,367
Always?

204
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:00,287
From the first day we met?

205
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:02,414
This whole time?

206
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,918
Thank you so much.

207
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:09,630
It's because I'm self-centered.

208
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:13,509
Honestly, it doesn't matter
what anyone else says or thinks,

209
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:16,053
there's always a part of me
that just doesn't care.

210
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:21,266
I think it's really rare
to find people you can truly open up to.

211
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:23,018
I guess

212
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:27,272
that's why I have a tendency
to keep people at arm's length.

213
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:32,569
For a while,
it was just instinct, I think.

214
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:34,655
But, I...

215
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:39,159
I just can't stay away from you,
no matter what.

216
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:42,412
I care about everything you say and think.

217
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:45,207
It's embarrassing, but...

218
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:49,044
I really wanted to play it cool.

219
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:55,050
Until I met you... I had no idea
that I was this kind of person.

220
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:12,484
This is a Kazehaya I have never known.

221
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:16,363
When I first met you...

222
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:22,494
If you happen to be looking for
Kitahoro High and you're lost,

223
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:23,495
it's that way.

224
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:27,583
Has something been... bothering you?

225
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:33,213
I can't.

226
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,508
If I get too close, I'll...

227
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,802
Is that cool?

228
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:41,805
If I borrow Sadako to talk alone.

229
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:44,099
Ya dumb jerk.

230
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:47,269
If that's how you're gonna put it,
of course I'd wanna say no.

231
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,148
I...

232
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:55,360
The thing about me is I'm a petty guy.

233
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,155
So damn petty.

234
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:01,158
- That's amazing!
- Huh?

235
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:04,620
Thanks, Sadako.
You made it so easy to understand.

236
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:07,664
Thank you, Sadako!

237
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:14,087
I wanna see her smile.

238
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:18,133
When I'm happy for her, it's real.

239
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:21,428
But...

240
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:25,390
I want her for myself.

241
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:29,895
I know... that's not something I can have.

242
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,023
If I just took what I wanted,

243
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:35,734
then all their hard work
would have been for nothing.

244
00:20:38,111 --> 00:20:41,823
My life would be completely different
without you in it, Kazehaya.

245
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:46,411
That's funny.

246
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:50,374
I'm the one who should be saying that.

247
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:55,170
- Each time we encounter each other...
- Hm?

248
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,631
...I'm the one...

249
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:02,052
...who falls even deeper.

250
00:21:04,429 --> 00:21:06,765
The thing is... I, uh...

251
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:10,644
I don't know
if the "me" that you see even exists.

252
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:15,649
The version of Kazehaya
that I see is...

253
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,568
...so refreshing, right down to your name.

254
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:24,616
Truth is, I have zero intention
of ever giving you up.

255
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:26,702
I like you.

256
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:28,662
But in spite of that,

257
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:31,039
or maybe because of it...

258
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:38,297
...I don't know
if I could cherish you how you deserve.

259
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:40,841
But even so,

260
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:43,885
I don't ever wanna let you go.

261
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:49,141
Even if it means... I might end up
becoming your greatest source of pain.

262
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,603
Kazehaya.

263
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:55,897
Don't you see it?

264
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:58,900
You deserve to be
with somebody who's worthy of you.

265
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,695
I don't know
if that's a scary, selfish guy like me.

266
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:04,323
Kazehaya...

267
00:22:05,907 --> 00:22:07,951
I know you could do so much better.

268
00:22:22,966 --> 00:22:24,468
Do you honestly not see it?

269
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:29,139
He says he's self-centered.

270
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:32,976
He doesn't know
how happy his genuine smile makes me.

271
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,772
How happy it makes all those around him.

272
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,274
He says he's scary.

273
00:22:41,651 --> 00:22:46,907
But right now, he doesn't have any idea
how glad I am to hear him say those words.

274
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:52,412
The only one who could hurt me
so deeply... is you.

275
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:54,164
And I'm fully aware of that.

276
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:58,460
Because only you can reach this deep
into my heart.

277
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:02,506
I think it's okay if things get awkward

278
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:04,674
or if we have a fight.

279
00:23:05,884 --> 00:23:10,347
'Cause even when things
are hard or there's conflict...

280
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:16,144
I'll still want to be with you.

281
00:23:18,271 --> 00:23:20,107
I don't care if it's not right.

282
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:35,455
If always chasing after someone
without ever reaching them

283
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:38,041
is unrequited love...

284
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:47,008
then, in truth, the two of us
should be able to stand face-to-face

285
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,386
and look each other in the eye.

286
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:06,319
If we can stand together
and face these challenges side-by-side,

287
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:08,613
then our love will flourish.

288
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,633
Sorry. Just this time.

289
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:48,820
- Hey, Kazehaya?
- Huh?

290
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:51,573
Y'know how
you keep insisting you're different

291
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:53,950
from whatever version
of you I'm perceiving?

292
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:56,161
Well...

293
00:24:58,163 --> 00:25:00,290
I'm pretty sure I'm not wrong about this.

294
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,834
You see, I can just tell.

295
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:06,588
Every single thing
you do and say feels genuine to me.

296
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:17,057
It's okay if I'm not right.

297
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:21,895
Even if none of it is right, all of it is.

298
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:31,571
Here's the thing about Shota.
He's narrow-minded and stubborn.

299
00:25:34,157 --> 00:25:36,243
If he's made up his mind, it's over.

300
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:38,286
The kid's head
is harder than a brick wall.

301
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,497
Deep down, he's really tough on himself.

302
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:42,123
And on others.

303
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:44,960
Well, not that that's a bad thing.

304
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:48,922
If only he'd learn
how to vent and let it all out!

305
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:51,508
See? I happen to be a master of the art.

306
00:25:52,092 --> 00:25:54,803
If you cannot contend
with the weaknesses in yourself,

307
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:57,639
then how could you do so
with the weaknesses in others?

308
00:25:57,722 --> 00:25:59,766
Hey! Did you hear a word I just said?!

309
00:25:59,849 --> 00:26:04,229
- And why aren't you writing this down!
- Oh. My. Gosh!

310
00:26:04,312 --> 00:26:07,566
How am I supposed to enjoy my ramen
when you won't shut up?!

311
00:26:07,649 --> 00:26:08,483
Watch it!

312
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,944
- You should be grateful for my wisdom.
- What?

313
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:12,612
Really, Pin?

314
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:15,907
You enjoy ambushing students
with lectures at Christmastime, huh?

315
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:16,908
Damn right!

316
00:26:16,992 --> 00:26:19,035
Now, let me hear you kids say thank you!

317
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:20,829
You two were wandering aimlessly.

318
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:23,582
Right up until I blessed you
with my great knowledge.

319
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:24,874
Merry Christmas!

320
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:27,210
Right, then.

321
00:26:27,294 --> 00:26:29,754
You two should
probably help Shota open up.

322
00:26:29,838 --> 00:26:33,049
Yeah, right!
If he opens up to anyone, it'll be Sawa!

323
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:38,805
Argh! Why is everything so hard!

324
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:41,099
Jeez, what's her problem?

325
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:43,977
Christmas spirit burning too hot? Ha!

326
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:50,942
I wonder if, somewhere in me,

327
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:53,445
those strong feelings
of longing are still there.

328
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:58,700
I always believed that
once two people became intimate,

329
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:01,995
they'd never have to worry
about the distance between them again.

330
00:27:04,122 --> 00:27:05,540
Guess I was wrong.

331
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:11,171
The more you like them,
the more you worry.

332
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,049
About all the ways
they keep their distance.

333
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:17,761
About every gesture and every
little change in their expression.

334
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:22,641
And because you like them,

335
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:27,062
every last little detail
doesn't matter anymore.

336
00:27:31,816 --> 00:27:32,776
Please.

337
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:35,487
Please.

338
00:27:37,822 --> 00:27:40,867
Let us always have faith
in our feelings for each other.

339
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,872
You're not the only one
learning about yourself.

340
00:27:46,831 --> 00:27:49,209
The truth is, I am too.

341
00:27:49,959 --> 00:27:50,794
Huh?

342
00:27:52,420 --> 00:27:55,131
Sometimes,
I get jealous of the boys.

343
00:27:59,094 --> 00:28:00,512
It's true, I do.

344
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,139
I can get really possessive.

345
00:28:03,765 --> 00:28:05,558
Like, really possessive.

346
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:14,192
Kazehaya... I can walk the rest of the way.

347
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:16,027
What? But we're almost there?

348
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:41,052
I'm sorry I yelled and called you a liar!

349
00:28:54,941 --> 00:28:58,486
Why apologize? I am a liar.

350
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:02,824
I'm home!

351
00:29:02,907 --> 00:29:05,034
Oh, Sawako. You're back.

352
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:08,121
My, you're home
sooner than expected.

353
00:29:08,204 --> 00:29:10,999
What are you talking about?
She only had five minutes left, you know?

354
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:13,585
I didn't think she'd care
about the time limit.

355
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:15,128
Wha-- Huh?

356
00:29:18,089 --> 00:29:20,091
Did Kazehaya walk you home?

357
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:21,676
Mm-hmm.

358
00:29:22,385 --> 00:29:24,012
I'm sorry I stayed out late.

359
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:26,931
No, everything's fine!
You kept your promise, after all.

360
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:30,560
Besides, it's the holidays. It's special.

361
00:29:31,394 --> 00:29:32,562
You look freezing.

362
00:29:33,229 --> 00:29:35,857
Come on, hop into the bath
before you catch a cold.

363
00:29:39,527 --> 00:29:40,487
'Kay.

364
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:05,678
The last secret... of my 16th year.

365
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:36,167
Kazehaya, you lied. You're a liar!

366
00:30:36,751 --> 00:30:38,670
Is being with me
what's been bothering you?

367
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:42,090
You don't like me as I am anymore?

368
00:30:44,801 --> 00:30:45,844
Only you could hurt me.

369
00:30:47,303 --> 00:30:49,430
I'm sorry I yelled and called you a liar!

370
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:53,476
I'll never get to sleep.

371
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:54,686
INCOMING CALL

372
00:30:54,769 --> 00:30:55,603
Hmm?

373
00:30:57,897 --> 00:30:59,649
Who's calling at this hour?

374
00:31:02,902 --> 00:31:04,153
Yes? Uh, hello?

375
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:06,114
Kazehaya! What's good?

376
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:07,615
CLICK

377
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:09,701
Hung up without thinking.

378
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:13,162
Wha-- Who's this?

379
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:16,291
Um, hello?

380
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,376
That hurt my feelings, you know?

381
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,627
Hanging up like that.

382
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:21,421
It's your old buddy Kent--

383
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:26,843
Hello?

384
00:31:26,926 --> 00:31:28,803
- Kazehaya!
- Sorry.

385
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:31,264
- That was so mean!
- I said I'm sorry.

386
00:31:31,347 --> 00:31:33,600
So, I guess you can do whatever you want,

387
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:35,768
no matter how
it might affect someone else.

388
00:31:35,852 --> 00:31:39,022
This coming from the guy
who's calling me at 2:30 in the morning?

389
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:43,151
Still, for some reason,

390
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:45,528
connecting with the guy
feels strangely easy.

391
00:31:46,154 --> 00:31:47,488
So, what's up?

392
00:31:47,572 --> 00:31:51,200
Oh, you know,
just doing my duty and reporting in.

393
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:52,994
Like a good friend would!

394
00:31:53,077 --> 00:31:54,454
What are you talking about?

395
00:31:54,537 --> 00:31:58,917
Ooh, want the details?
You're so hopeless, Kazehaya.

396
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,419
Will you stop? Let's hear it.

397
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:03,463
Well, here goes...

398
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:07,717
As of this moment,
I'm officially going out with Ayane!

399
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:10,428
Huh?

400
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:12,472
Uh...

401
00:32:13,139 --> 00:32:14,474
Oh!

402
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:15,683
Hold on.

403
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,560
Did you hear something from Sadako?

404
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:21,230
Uh, no, she didn't tell me anything.

405
00:32:22,398 --> 00:32:23,483
I see.

406
00:32:23,566 --> 00:32:25,318
Gotcha.

407
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:28,488
I'm happy for you.

408
00:32:31,783 --> 00:32:35,036
To be honest,
I wasn't as smooth as I wanted to be.

409
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:37,080
I got her a bouquet of roses,

410
00:32:37,163 --> 00:32:39,374
but then Joe went
and stepped on it.

411
00:32:39,457 --> 00:32:41,084
Did you say a bouquet of roses?!

412
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:43,252
Totally seems like her thing, right?

413
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:48,132
The reddest I could find.
I was a nervous wreck.

414
00:32:50,259 --> 00:32:52,887
By the way, I ran into Mogi-cchi today.

415
00:32:53,554 --> 00:32:54,389
Uh-huh.

416
00:32:54,472 --> 00:32:57,809
- And I kinda decked him in the schnoz.
- Uh-huh.

417
00:32:58,434 --> 00:33:00,603
Wait a sec, you're not surprised?

418
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:01,896
Why'd you hit him?

419
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,856
Oh, I'm not one to punch and tell!

420
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:05,650
Goodbye.

421
00:33:05,733 --> 00:33:09,487
Well, long story short,
he said some things about Ayane

422
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:12,699
that I just couldn't let slide...
so I didn't.

423
00:33:12,782 --> 00:33:13,616
Mmm.

424
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:17,578
Thinking back on it, it was probably
jealousy that drove me to do it.

425
00:33:19,622 --> 00:33:20,873
I'm curious.

426
00:33:20,957 --> 00:33:23,584
- You think I made a difference?
- Mm-hmm.

427
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:27,255
So, the two of you are a couple now,
aren't you?

428
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:31,634
You're gonna show her a good time
and treat her like a princess, right?

429
00:33:33,052 --> 00:33:35,013
Mmm.

430
00:33:35,596 --> 00:33:36,472
How about you?

431
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,558
Me? I, uh...

432
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:39,559
What am I saying?

433
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:41,936
- I'm not worried about you two at all.
- What?!

434
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:45,481
Remember what I said
the last time you called me for advice?

435
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:48,776
You and sweet Sadako
have absolutely nothing to worry about.

436
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:52,071
When did I ask him for advice?

437
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:54,198
But, let's get back to Ayane.

438
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:55,241
Uh, sure?

439
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:59,912
She's so adorable and so kind too.
There's a million reasons to love her.

440
00:33:59,996 --> 00:34:02,749
I'm tellin' ya, nobody knows the real her.

441
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:05,918
There are guys out there who would
write off a girl so sweet and gorgeous

442
00:34:06,002 --> 00:34:08,129
and awesome and cool, can you believe it?!

443
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:09,797
What's wrong with people these days?

444
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:12,383
I mean, I guess there's no helping
terrible taste, but still,

445
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:14,093
it totally boggles my mind.

446
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:16,721
Honestly, I could go on about
the things to love about her.

447
00:34:16,804 --> 00:34:20,099
I could start right now and keep going
for hours, maybe even days.

448
00:34:20,183 --> 00:34:22,393
Even after that,
I could come up with new stuff.

449
00:34:22,477 --> 00:34:25,354
- Hey, you there, buddy?
- Huh?! Yeah. Yep.

450
00:34:26,647 --> 00:34:28,357
I can say it. At last.

451
00:34:29,692 --> 00:34:32,195
I know what love is!

452
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:36,657
Yi... yippee.

453
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:57,386
Until last year, I always woke up
to a present next to my pillow.

454
00:35:03,851 --> 00:35:06,729
Here's a sign
that it wasn't all just a dream.

455
00:35:10,525 --> 00:35:11,734
Good morning!

456
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,529
- There you are. Good morning, dear.
- Hey, kiddo.

457
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:16,656
Sawako!

458
00:35:16,739 --> 00:35:20,409
Did you think your father and I had
forgotten about your Christmas present?

459
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:26,749
Oh, thank you!

460
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:29,252
The scarf was personally chosen
by yours truly.

461
00:35:29,335 --> 00:35:33,256
What an incredible coincidence
because I got you a scarf too!

462
00:35:33,339 --> 00:35:35,716
- You did what?!
- Here.

463
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:38,386
- We're... in... sync!
- We're... in... sync!

464
00:35:39,595 --> 00:35:42,223
I'm so happy for you, honey.

465
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:44,767
And thank you for the shawl. I love it.

466
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:48,354
Oh, it pains me to have to leave,
but work's calling.

467
00:35:48,437 --> 00:35:49,772
I must get going.

468
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:52,900
Oh, let's have our party
the moment I get home, okay?

469
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:55,403
Right then, ladies. I'm off!

470
00:35:55,486 --> 00:35:57,405
See you tonight.

471
00:35:58,072 --> 00:36:00,700
Come on, hun.
You should go finish your breakfast.

472
00:36:00,783 --> 00:36:01,617
Mm-hmm.

473
00:36:02,410 --> 00:36:03,619
Oh.

474
00:36:06,122 --> 00:36:07,415
A text message?

475
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:12,879
Coming!

476
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:14,172
- We're here!
- We're here!

477
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:16,549
Make yourself at home.

478
00:36:17,633 --> 00:36:18,551
Welcome.

479
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:20,344
Thanks for having us!

480
00:36:21,804 --> 00:36:23,890
We texted you pretty last-minute.

481
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:26,350
You sure us dropping by
isn't too much trouble?

482
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:29,520
No, not at all. I'm glad.

483
00:36:30,646 --> 00:36:34,233
We didn't really get to talk much
yesterday, but now's our chance.

484
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:37,486
You're right! Holy crap,
I've got so much to tell you!

485
00:36:37,570 --> 00:36:40,573
Argh! Where do I begin?!

486
00:36:40,656 --> 00:36:42,241
Try sitting down first?

487
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:45,578
I have news too.

488
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:54,086
I was thinking, we could take some time
to catch each other up on our lives.

489
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:12,021
Uh, why is everybody so quiet?
Someone say something or I'll explode!

490
00:37:12,104 --> 00:37:14,941
Um, I mean,
you seemed the most eager to share,

491
00:37:15,024 --> 00:37:17,193
so we were just waiting
for you to say something.

492
00:37:24,325 --> 00:37:26,535
Oh wow. That's a lotta sweat.

493
00:37:27,036 --> 00:37:28,246
Hey! Sawa!

494
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:30,164
I thought you had news to report?

495
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:32,750
The floor is yours! Go!

496
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:44,804
So, yesterday,

497
00:37:45,596 --> 00:37:48,266
I cried and told him
I was having some doubts.

498
00:37:49,433 --> 00:37:52,395
But... we're all better now.

499
00:37:53,020 --> 00:37:54,563
You had doubts?

500
00:37:54,647 --> 00:37:56,399
Wait! This is massive!

501
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,694
I see. You talked after the party, huh?

502
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:02,571
Mm-hmm. It was past my curfew.

503
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:05,574
But, I'm glad we stayed out.

504
00:38:08,577 --> 00:38:12,665
Because I... I think,
thanks to our conversation,

505
00:38:12,748 --> 00:38:15,459
us being together
finally feels real to me.

506
00:38:19,338 --> 00:38:21,674
- Good for you.
- Good for you.

507
00:38:21,757 --> 00:38:24,093
But what does she mean by doubts?!

508
00:38:24,176 --> 00:38:25,136
I just don't get it!

509
00:38:25,219 --> 00:38:29,181
Your relationship with Kazehaya's always
been clear skies and smooth talking!

510
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:31,559
"Smooth sailing," not talking.

511
00:38:31,642 --> 00:38:33,102
But why did you cry?

512
00:38:33,185 --> 00:38:35,313
Why'd you have doubts?!

513
00:38:36,897 --> 00:38:38,482
Wait, so there is something?

514
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:43,237
Come to think of it, it totally seems
like something is bothering Kazehaya.

515
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:47,950
Now... it... all makes sense!

516
00:38:48,034 --> 00:38:49,827
I really am sorry, Chizu!

517
00:38:49,910 --> 00:38:53,372
Wait! Did Kazehaya cheat on you
even though you're way out of his league?

518
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:57,126
- That good-for-nothing little--
- Cheat on me? There's no way!

519
00:38:57,209 --> 00:38:59,879
He would never do that to me!
Not in a million years!

520
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:01,839
That's her first thought?

521
00:39:05,217 --> 00:39:07,511
That's how badly
communication broke down?

522
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:09,263
Yano-chin, did you know this?

523
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:12,516
Yeah, I was aware, but timing-wise,
it was a bit tricky.

524
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:16,604
You see, this was right after
you ran off to buy Ryu's present.

525
00:39:16,687 --> 00:39:18,522
That's when she told me about it.

526
00:39:20,149 --> 00:39:22,193
- So how about you, Chizu?
- Huh?

527
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:28,240
I know something happened
between you and Ryu.

528
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:30,409
Since you never came back to the party.

529
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:35,039
I mean, yeah,
something did happen, but, uh...

530
00:39:35,122 --> 00:39:39,126
Hey, I don't think I like the way
you guys are staring at me. Um...

531
00:39:40,002 --> 00:39:41,087
Gah!

532
00:39:41,170 --> 00:39:43,589
I need time to prepare myself emotionally!

533
00:39:43,672 --> 00:39:44,507
Sure.

534
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:46,926
In that case,
I suppose I'll just go first.

535
00:39:51,138 --> 00:39:53,599
Kento and I are now dating.

536
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,227
Ayane!

537
00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:59,897
After a while, it starts to feel
like every guy'll be the same.

538
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:02,691
That I'll never have anything serious.

539
00:40:02,775 --> 00:40:06,153
I can't help it. That's just how I feel.

540
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:09,615
Have you ever...
stopped to consider

541
00:40:10,574 --> 00:40:13,077
how that behavior
might have made her feel?!

542
00:40:13,661 --> 00:40:16,205
I'll be the one to comfort her.

543
00:40:16,997 --> 00:40:18,290
Master...

544
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:21,043
you reached her!

545
00:40:23,504 --> 00:40:25,423
I'm so happy for you!

546
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:31,303
Huh? Wait, you said Kento?!

547
00:40:31,887 --> 00:40:34,598
That doofus
is your boyfriend?!

548
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:36,934
Yes, I'm referring to that Kento.

549
00:40:37,017 --> 00:40:38,519
But why that idiot?!

550
00:40:39,186 --> 00:40:40,354
Oh right.

551
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:42,940
I forgot she doesn't know
about any of this yet.

552
00:40:43,023 --> 00:40:45,943
Ah, I see. This is all just a dream!

553
00:40:46,026 --> 00:40:47,445
Sorry, it's all real.

554
00:40:47,528 --> 00:40:48,946
That really hurts.

555
00:40:50,030 --> 00:40:52,533
Now that I think about it,
back at the start of second year,

556
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:55,119
there was a time
you couldn't shut up about Kento!

557
00:40:55,202 --> 00:40:57,037
Were you two already a thing then?

558
00:40:57,121 --> 00:40:59,081
Not at all.
That was something else.

559
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:02,918
Wait, doesn't this surprise you?

560
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:09,258
Have I been that clueless
this entire time?

561
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:14,054
Well, yeah, you were. So clueless.

562
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:17,850
At the start
of the Christmas party yesterday,

563
00:41:17,933 --> 00:41:19,852
you two weren't a couple yet, right?

564
00:41:19,935 --> 00:41:21,312
What the heck happened?

565
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:24,607
Uh, well, you see...

566
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:27,318
Truth is, it didn't exactly
come out of nowhere.

567
00:41:29,195 --> 00:41:32,281
During free activities time
on our class trip,

568
00:41:32,364 --> 00:41:36,827
Kento and I bumped into each other
after I had just broken up with Mogi.

569
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:39,580
I kind of started crying.

570
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:43,709
Not because I was sad over the breakup.

571
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:47,421
I think I might've
accidentally let my guard down a little.

572
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:52,426
But even so,
I don't think it was a mistake.

573
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:57,097
Whenever he's around, I start to relax.

574
00:41:57,723 --> 00:42:00,559
Honestly, he's a really sweet guy.

575
00:42:01,685 --> 00:42:05,147
Still, I can't help but wonder
if I made the right call.

576
00:42:05,231 --> 00:42:07,566
Huh? Did you just
suddenly realize he sucks?

577
00:42:07,650 --> 00:42:10,819
What?! No!
I genuinely think he's a great guy.

578
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:16,909
In fact, he's nothing like any of the
other guys I've gone out with so far.

579
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:20,621
I guess that's why

580
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:23,290
I was so touched.

581
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:28,420
Sawako, if you asked me right now

582
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:31,090
if I liked Kento
the same way you like Kazehaya,

583
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:33,717
I honestly couldn't tell you.

584
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:37,930
But this is the first time
anyone's been so passionate about me

585
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:41,100
and so determined to stand up for me.

586
00:42:42,101 --> 00:42:44,270
It made me ridiculously happy.

587
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:47,731
So, no, I don't think he sucks at all.

588
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:53,654
The thing is,
I don't have that much faith in myself.

589
00:42:53,737 --> 00:42:56,740
So the issue isn't Kento. It's me.

590
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:59,660
That's why I keep wondering
if this was the right choice.

591
00:42:59,743 --> 00:43:03,372
- Course everything's fine!
- You did another one-eighty.

592
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:06,584
Okay, look, I can't say I really get it.

593
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:10,129
If I'm being honest, I can't name
a single thing I like about the guy.

594
00:43:10,754 --> 00:43:13,048
But if his is the shoulder
you wanna cry on,

595
00:43:13,132 --> 00:43:14,508
then fine, I'll share you.

596
00:43:15,342 --> 00:43:18,762
And when that's over with,
I'll still be here! 'Kay?

597
00:43:18,846 --> 00:43:20,598
Way to jinx it!

598
00:43:21,765 --> 00:43:24,184
Still, thanks, I guess.

599
00:43:32,651 --> 00:43:33,485
Well?

600
00:43:33,569 --> 00:43:34,862
Eh?

601
00:43:34,945 --> 00:43:36,947
- Well?
- Eh?

602
00:43:37,031 --> 00:43:38,032
- Well?
- Mm-hmm?

603
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:39,658
Eh?

604
00:43:46,498 --> 00:43:48,667
It's your turn now. Go ahead.

605
00:43:49,418 --> 00:43:52,379
You seriously expect me
to follow those two stories?

606
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:54,298
C'mon, how am I supposed to do that?

607
00:43:54,381 --> 00:43:57,760
You're not getting off the hook.
We want every detail.

608
00:43:57,843 --> 00:44:01,847
I should have gone first.

609
00:44:03,390 --> 00:44:04,266
Anyway...

610
00:44:06,518 --> 00:44:08,979
this is one of those, uh, pickled flowers.

611
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:12,274
"Pickled flower"?

612
00:44:12,358 --> 00:44:15,194
Uh, yeah! They do that thing
to make it last longer.

613
00:44:15,277 --> 00:44:17,029
Do you mean a preserved flower?

614
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:18,989
Oh! Uh, yeah, that.

615
00:44:19,073 --> 00:44:21,033
Wow, look at that.

616
00:44:21,116 --> 00:44:23,285
Yeah, a lovely pink rose!

617
00:44:23,869 --> 00:44:26,413
Isn't it... so very pink?

618
00:44:26,497 --> 00:44:28,207
Very, very pink!

619
00:44:31,085 --> 00:44:32,086
Huh?

620
00:44:33,879 --> 00:44:35,839
Does it remind you of me?

621
00:44:37,424 --> 00:44:39,259
Tell me. Does it?

622
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:42,054
- Do you think of me when you see it?
- Mmmmm!

623
00:44:42,137 --> 00:44:44,098
It's so you! It's very you!

624
00:44:44,181 --> 00:44:47,101
Chizu, your pupils are
very dilated right now.

625
00:44:49,478 --> 00:44:52,439
So anyway, what did you do
after he gave you this?

626
00:44:52,523 --> 00:44:54,525
Huh? What do you mean, what did I do?

627
00:44:54,608 --> 00:44:57,486
Do I have to spell it out?
This is a pink rose!

628
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:59,446
- A pi-- pickled--
- Preserved!

629
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,532
So, did you just accept it
and leave it at that,

630
00:45:01,615 --> 00:45:03,158
or did something else happen?

631
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:05,411
Huh?! Well, I gave him a present!

632
00:45:05,994 --> 00:45:07,871
I, uh, stole it back from Joe.

633
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:10,040
But yeah, I, uh...

634
00:45:10,124 --> 00:45:13,085
- I sorta feel bad for the guy.
- No need to worry.

635
00:45:13,168 --> 00:45:16,338
Ayane didn't miss a beat
and gave Joe her rock salt.

636
00:45:16,422 --> 00:45:18,173
Whoa! Thank you, Yano-chin!

637
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:20,676
Let's not get sidetracked!

638
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:23,095
The two of you suddenly disappeared

639
00:45:23,178 --> 00:45:26,557
for a suspiciously long
stretch of time during the party.

640
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:29,184
I wanna know what happened. Now!

641
00:45:29,768 --> 00:45:31,854
We just talked about normal stuff,

642
00:45:31,937 --> 00:45:34,106
like what we'd had
for dinner last night, and...

643
00:45:34,189 --> 00:45:35,983
After you got this?

644
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:37,818
...and TV shows...

645
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:39,445
After you got this?

646
00:45:40,195 --> 00:45:41,905
...and ramen...

647
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:45,033
Really? After you got this pink rose?!

648
00:45:49,371 --> 00:45:51,749
You... you did
naughty adult things!

649
00:45:51,832 --> 00:45:53,000
That has to be it!

650
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:01,550
We talked about when we were kids.

651
00:46:02,301 --> 00:46:03,677
About Toru.

652
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:06,638
And about his late mother.

653
00:46:07,806 --> 00:46:10,058
But there's just never enough time.

654
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:11,977
We share so many memories.

655
00:46:12,811 --> 00:46:16,231
It's been so long since we got
to sit down and talk like that.

656
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:20,527
Oh yeah. He mentioned Toru's
gonna be home for New Year's.

657
00:46:21,153 --> 00:46:25,532
- Is he really? You gonna see him?
- Yeah, I'd like that.

658
00:46:25,616 --> 00:46:28,619
See him again.
And look him in the face, y'know?

659
00:46:28,702 --> 00:46:30,078
- Mm-mmm!
- Mm-mmm!

660
00:46:30,662 --> 00:46:31,872
Hm?

661
00:46:31,955 --> 00:46:33,248
- Mm-mmm!
- Mm-mmm!

662
00:46:35,334 --> 00:46:38,837
Of course! She wants to go meet
her first love face-to-face

663
00:46:38,921 --> 00:46:41,423
and see for herself
whether there are lingering feelings.

664
00:46:41,507 --> 00:46:42,716
Wait! But that's not it!

665
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,552
Man! I gotta say I'm surprised.

666
00:46:45,636 --> 00:46:47,805
I'd never expect this
from someone like Ryu.

667
00:46:47,888 --> 00:46:50,224
He picked it 'cause it made him
think of Chizu.

668
00:46:52,226 --> 00:46:54,770
So tell me.
Whenever you're alone with him...

669
00:46:54,853 --> 00:46:56,104
...does your heart go "bwaa"?

670
00:46:58,649 --> 00:46:59,483
I...

671
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:03,612
For the first time in my life,

672
00:47:03,695 --> 00:47:06,657
whenever I see that boy,
my heart starts racing.

673
00:47:06,740 --> 00:47:08,450
SQUEE!

674
00:47:08,534 --> 00:47:10,702
Goodness, it sounds like
they're having fun.

675
00:47:10,786 --> 00:47:14,706
Anyway, what about you two?
Did you get presents?

676
00:47:14,790 --> 00:47:15,833
Yeah.

677
00:47:15,916 --> 00:47:17,668
Uh-huh. Me too.

678
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:23,382
Oh wow, I love them.
They're so cute and totally you.

679
00:47:23,465 --> 00:47:27,344
One hundred percent.
Good job, Kazehaya, you Sawako fanatic!

680
00:47:27,928 --> 00:47:30,138
I think he's earned himself
a thank-you kiss!

681
00:47:32,182 --> 00:47:33,183
- Huh?
- Huh?

682
00:47:33,267 --> 00:47:34,351
- Did you?
- Did you?

683
00:47:34,434 --> 00:47:35,811
- Did you?!
- Did you?!

684
00:47:35,894 --> 00:47:38,689
I can neither confirm nor deny.

685
00:47:38,772 --> 00:47:40,190
- That's mean!
- Oh, c'mon!

686
00:47:40,274 --> 00:47:44,194
I won't. And there's nothing you could say
or do to convince me otherwise.

687
00:47:45,320 --> 00:47:46,780
- Then, how 'bout you?
- Huh?

688
00:47:46,864 --> 00:47:49,241
What romantic gift did you get from Kento?

689
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:51,869
R-- roses.

690
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:54,204
Oh, enough about the rose!
I'm asking what you got!

691
00:47:54,288 --> 00:47:57,541
I know! Kento got me roses.
A whole bouquet, in fact.

692
00:47:57,624 --> 00:47:58,709
A bouquet!

693
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:00,919
Deep-red ones.

694
00:48:01,461 --> 00:48:04,047
You... You're sure we're talking about
the same Kento,

695
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,841
the Japanese high-schooler?

696
00:48:05,924 --> 00:48:10,053
Totally. Kento Miura.
Age sixteen, second year.

697
00:48:10,137 --> 00:48:13,015
- Gotta see it!
- Sure. I took some pictures.

698
00:48:14,641 --> 00:48:17,102
Whoa, you're right!
Those are red as hell!

699
00:48:17,185 --> 00:48:19,313
Yep, and there's white
on the petals too.

700
00:48:19,396 --> 00:48:20,522
That's so cute!

701
00:48:20,606 --> 00:48:22,983
Yeah, but why are
the petals all scattered?

702
00:48:23,066 --> 00:48:25,193
Because Joe
stepped on the bouquet.

703
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:27,279
Are-- are you serious? That jerk.

704
00:48:27,362 --> 00:48:30,782
The instant I undid the wrapping,
it fell to pieces.

705
00:48:31,325 --> 00:48:32,784
So I put them in a bowl.

706
00:48:33,911 --> 00:48:37,289
Kento says that this rose
might stop existing in ten years.

707
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:38,540
Wait, why?

708
00:48:38,624 --> 00:48:40,125
Well, apparently,

709
00:48:40,208 --> 00:48:43,545
the florist told him that
the farmer who grows them is getting old.

710
00:48:43,629 --> 00:48:46,423
Makes me wonder if a farmer
somewhere else is growing them.

711
00:48:46,506 --> 00:48:49,551
I thought about that too.

712
00:48:50,135 --> 00:48:53,764
Ten years from now...
I wonder what I'll be doing.

713
00:48:53,847 --> 00:48:55,223
Ten years!

714
00:48:55,307 --> 00:48:58,018
That's so far away,
I can't picture it, you know.

715
00:48:58,101 --> 00:49:01,271
We'll be 27!
Maybe we'll all be married by then.

716
00:49:01,355 --> 00:49:03,231
We might even have kids.

717
00:49:03,857 --> 00:49:05,067
Ten years.

718
00:49:07,444 --> 00:49:09,154
Ten years from now.

719
00:49:10,906 --> 00:49:12,616
Ten whole years.

720
00:49:15,327 --> 00:49:18,580
I sure hope we'll still be able
to spend time together.

721
00:49:26,380 --> 00:49:28,882
What are you talking about?!
We'll be together forever!

722
00:49:28,966 --> 00:49:30,133
Absolutely.

723
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:33,845
It's lunchtime, girls!

724
00:49:33,929 --> 00:49:35,097
Yay, lunch!

725
00:49:35,180 --> 00:49:36,515
Thank you so much!

726
00:49:37,224 --> 00:49:39,559
Nothing fancy.
Just rice balls and soup.

727
00:49:39,643 --> 00:49:42,396
- Thanks, Mom!
- Don't mention it.

728
00:49:42,479 --> 00:49:46,066
For me, ten years ago
feels like yesterday.

729
00:49:46,149 --> 00:49:48,610
I love seeing how excited you are.

730
00:49:48,694 --> 00:49:52,698
Yano-chin went and got herself
a boyfriend, and he gave her fancy roses!

731
00:49:52,781 --> 00:49:55,575
So did Chizu. He gave her this.

732
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,786
But he's not officially her boyfriend yet.

733
00:49:57,869 --> 00:50:00,080
How absolutely gorgeous.

734
00:50:00,163 --> 00:50:02,666
I haven't had this kind of girl talk
in so long.

735
00:50:02,749 --> 00:50:05,085
I bet it's 'cause
Sawako doesn't like to share.

736
00:50:05,168 --> 00:50:07,462
It's not like that at all!

737
00:50:08,338 --> 00:50:10,424
Talking with Chizu and Ayane,

738
00:50:10,507 --> 00:50:12,759
sharing pieces of our lives
with each other,

739
00:50:12,843 --> 00:50:14,678
and even having lunch together...

740
00:50:15,804 --> 00:50:17,180
It's such a perfect day.

741
00:50:17,264 --> 00:50:20,434
Well, in that case, I think
they should stick around for dinner.

742
00:50:20,517 --> 00:50:21,560
What?!

743
00:50:21,643 --> 00:50:24,438
Yep! We're having
our Christmas party tonight.

744
00:50:24,521 --> 00:50:26,898
Sawako even baked a cake for the occasion.

745
00:50:26,982 --> 00:50:28,942
Wha-- She made a whole cake?

746
00:50:29,026 --> 00:50:30,527
I'd love it if you tried some.

747
00:50:30,610 --> 00:50:31,987
You sure that's okay?

748
00:50:32,070 --> 00:50:33,280
Wait a sec.

749
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:35,407
Can we really intrude on a family thing?

750
00:50:35,490 --> 00:50:36,324
Of course.

751
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:38,785
You know what they say.
The more, the merrier!

752
00:50:38,869 --> 00:50:41,621
Here's an idea. Why don't you
ask Kazehaya to come over?

753
00:50:42,914 --> 00:50:46,293
And why don't you two ladies
invite your boyfriends over too?

754
00:50:46,376 --> 00:50:47,210
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

755
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:49,463
- Oh, don't be shy.
- Go on!

756
00:50:56,970 --> 00:50:58,180
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

757
00:50:58,263 --> 00:51:00,766
Oh dear. Welcome, boys. Come on in!

758
00:51:01,349 --> 00:51:02,601
Thanks for having us.

759
00:51:14,905 --> 00:51:17,908
You brought it with you?
And you showed it to them?

760
00:51:18,784 --> 00:51:20,660
Uh... yeah.

761
00:51:20,744 --> 00:51:23,455
There's a million reasons
why I wish you hadn't done that.

762
00:51:23,538 --> 00:51:25,415
I... I'm sorry.

763
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:28,877
Is he mad?!

764
00:51:29,711 --> 00:51:32,380
I'm pretty embarrassed about it too.

765
00:51:32,964 --> 00:51:33,882
Gah!

766
00:51:35,217 --> 00:51:36,384
GURGLE

767
00:51:36,802 --> 00:51:37,844
I'm starving.

768
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:41,181
Th-- this way.
Make yourself at home, Kazehaya.

769
00:51:41,264 --> 00:51:43,058
Oh, yeah, thanks.

770
00:51:43,141 --> 00:51:44,142
Wait! Just a second!

771
00:51:45,227 --> 00:51:46,436
It slammed shut!

772
00:51:47,729 --> 00:51:51,191
Um, so,
did you really not have plans?

773
00:51:51,274 --> 00:51:53,693
Yeah. I was free. It's fine.

774
00:51:54,653 --> 00:51:57,030
And your family... doesn't mind?

775
00:51:57,656 --> 00:51:58,573
No, they don't.

776
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:03,453
Um... did you have trouble getting here?

777
00:52:03,537 --> 00:52:04,454
Nope, all good.

778
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,628
You don't have to worry.
Everything's fine.

779
00:52:17,843 --> 00:52:19,302
Uh, uh...

780
00:52:19,386 --> 00:52:20,595
Sorry, say that again?

781
00:52:21,138 --> 00:52:24,391
- Um, well, you see, I, uh...
- Huh?

782
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:31,398
It happened only yesterday, so...

783
00:52:33,275 --> 00:52:36,486
I thought I'd still be too shy
to say anything about it.

784
00:52:41,867 --> 00:52:43,618
It's not what you think!

785
00:52:43,702 --> 00:52:46,955
You were acting all sneaky,
so I kind of got curious.

786
00:52:47,038 --> 00:52:50,000
I think you're acting way more sneaky
than both of them are.

787
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:58,175
It's hard to believe
that just yesterday,

788
00:52:58,258 --> 00:53:00,218
we couldn't look each other in the eye.

789
00:53:01,970 --> 00:53:03,889
Hi! Pardon the intrusion!

790
00:53:03,972 --> 00:53:06,725
My yearning for Ayane
swept me to this place.

791
00:53:06,808 --> 00:53:09,394
- Oh my! Welcome!
- Master!

792
00:53:09,477 --> 00:53:12,480
Wow! Feels like forever
since we last talked.

793
00:53:12,564 --> 00:53:14,441
Is it because we've slept since then?

794
00:53:14,524 --> 00:53:15,817
Oh, I disagree.

795
00:53:15,901 --> 00:53:18,361
Must be something wrong
with your perception of time.

796
00:53:27,871 --> 00:53:28,705
Huh?

797
00:53:29,831 --> 00:53:30,665
Honey, I'm--

798
00:53:31,708 --> 00:53:34,127
- Welcome back!
- Welcome back!

799
00:53:34,211 --> 00:53:38,089
- Wha--
- C'mon! Hurry, Dad!

800
00:53:38,173 --> 00:53:39,799
Everything is ready!

801
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:43,220
It's good to see you again.
The whole gang is here tonight.

802
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:44,137
Oh.

803
00:53:44,221 --> 00:53:46,932
This guy and I
have been friends since forever.

804
00:53:47,015 --> 00:53:48,141
He's huge!

805
00:53:48,225 --> 00:53:50,185
And I'm Ayane's boyfriend.

806
00:53:50,268 --> 00:53:51,102
Slimy!

807
00:53:53,855 --> 00:53:57,108
- Hm?
- Th... thank you for having us.

808
00:53:57,192 --> 00:53:59,986
Last night, I'm sorry
we stayed out so late.

809
00:54:01,905 --> 00:54:04,241
Are you sure
you're serious about dating her?

810
00:54:05,450 --> 00:54:06,284
Yes.

811
00:54:09,913 --> 00:54:11,039
Fine, then.

812
00:54:13,250 --> 00:54:14,334
Hey, Dad!

813
00:54:14,417 --> 00:54:16,127
Here, let me take your bag.

814
00:54:16,211 --> 00:54:19,798
- Oh, right, here. It's strawberries.
- Ah, that's great!

815
00:54:19,881 --> 00:54:21,299
- Hm?
- Thanks, Dad!

816
00:54:25,011 --> 00:54:25,929
What the...

817
00:54:26,680 --> 00:54:30,892
Sawako, you've grown.
Like, a whole heck of a lot.

818
00:54:30,976 --> 00:54:32,560
Oh, have I?

819
00:54:33,186 --> 00:54:34,688
I'm going to go prepare these.

820
00:54:36,356 --> 00:54:37,190
Ahh.

821
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:39,067
- Oh, that hat!
- Huh?

822
00:54:39,150 --> 00:54:42,028
Sawako was gonna give that to Kazehaya--

823
00:54:42,112 --> 00:54:44,030
Mm-mm, mm-mm, mm-mm, mm-mm!

824
00:54:44,114 --> 00:54:46,157
Mwah. Merry Christmas!

825
00:54:46,241 --> 00:54:48,618
And a Happy New Year to you!

826
00:54:55,292 --> 00:54:58,169
Honey, come to the living room
once you've changed!

827
00:54:58,253 --> 00:54:59,421
Sure.

828
00:55:01,214 --> 00:55:03,633
So what do you
wanna do on the 31st?

829
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:05,719
Ooh! New Year's Eve plans?

830
00:55:05,802 --> 00:55:07,220
Oh, not just that!

831
00:55:07,304 --> 00:55:09,014
It's Sawako's birthday too.

832
00:55:09,097 --> 00:55:12,225
Wait, I had no idea you shared a birthday
with New Year's Eve.

833
00:55:12,309 --> 00:55:13,852
We totally need to celebrate!

834
00:55:13,935 --> 00:55:15,020
Aw!

835
00:55:15,103 --> 00:55:17,314
Everybody's being so nice!

836
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:20,066
Right, so we're all meeting up
for New Year's Eve.

837
00:55:20,150 --> 00:55:21,860
I think we should get together early.

838
00:55:21,943 --> 00:55:23,903
- Wait, I forgot to mention.
- Hm?

839
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:28,908
If it'll be at midnight...
then I can't make it.

840
00:55:29,868 --> 00:55:34,122
Last night, I got special permission
from my parents to stay out late,

841
00:55:34,205 --> 00:55:38,001
so I was going to say thank you
with toshikoshi soba noodles this year.

842
00:55:38,084 --> 00:55:40,462
Oh, is that a family favorite?

843
00:55:40,545 --> 00:55:43,256
If it's Sawako,
I bet she cooks 'em herself.

844
00:55:43,340 --> 00:55:46,259
None of that store-bought dashi
when she knows she could make her own.

845
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,927
- From scratch.
- Huh?

846
00:55:48,011 --> 00:55:51,139
- Making soba...
- From scratch, you say?

847
00:55:51,222 --> 00:55:54,934
This'll be my first time,
so I'm not sure they'll turn out too good.

848
00:55:58,104 --> 00:55:58,938
Hm.

849
00:56:01,900 --> 00:56:04,235
That's amazing!

850
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:08,490
Knowing you,
they'll come out perfect.

851
00:56:08,573 --> 00:56:09,491
Thanks!

852
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:12,577
Yo, Papan!

853
00:56:12,660 --> 00:56:15,121
What are you doing out here
all by your lonesome?

854
00:56:15,205 --> 00:56:17,665
Why don't you come over here and join us?

855
00:56:17,749 --> 00:56:19,125
Let me put this on you!

856
00:56:19,209 --> 00:56:20,126
Ta-dah!

857
00:56:20,210 --> 00:56:22,128
Argggggh!

858
00:56:25,799 --> 00:56:28,760
We went ahead and decked the halls
something fierce while waiting for you.

859
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:29,886
Check it out!

860
00:56:29,969 --> 00:56:32,347
Right, time to dig in, everyone.

861
00:56:33,014 --> 00:56:34,224
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

862
00:56:35,558 --> 00:56:36,434
Hey, Papa.

863
00:56:36,518 --> 00:56:39,813
Kazehaya's an incredibly nice guy,
isn't he, Sanada?

864
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:40,855
Ah, he's okay.

865
00:56:40,939 --> 00:56:44,734
Last night, he listened to me
ramble on and on until the sun came up.

866
00:56:44,818 --> 00:56:47,862
He did doze off a few times though,
which was super rude if you ask me.

867
00:56:47,946 --> 00:56:49,364
Are you serious?!

868
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:31,406
If we could all
keep spending time together like this,

869
00:57:31,489 --> 00:57:34,659
forever... how lovely would that be?

870
00:57:36,661 --> 00:57:39,581
- Thanks for having us.
- Everything was delicious.

871
00:57:39,664 --> 00:57:43,585
Sawa, I still gotta give you
your birthday gift, so I'll text you.

872
00:57:44,085 --> 00:57:45,920
Uh... okay, thank you!

873
00:57:46,504 --> 00:57:49,507
Me and Ayane are gonna head this way.

874
00:57:51,176 --> 00:57:52,010
Oh.

875
00:57:52,594 --> 00:57:55,638
Hey, uh... I gotta help my folks,

876
00:57:55,722 --> 00:57:58,850
so I may not have a lot of time
between now and New Year's Eve.

877
00:57:59,642 --> 00:58:02,228
But I can call you over winter break.

878
00:58:03,938 --> 00:58:07,150
Yeah, me too! I might text you
just to say hello sometimes.

879
00:58:07,233 --> 00:58:08,067
Cool.

880
00:58:09,027 --> 00:58:11,321
Maybe... I'll call too.

881
00:58:11,404 --> 00:58:13,364
Great. So will I.

882
00:58:20,205 --> 00:58:24,042
Sir, I'm sorry that
we all dropped by today unannounced.

883
00:58:25,043 --> 00:58:26,836
Thanks for your hospitality.

884
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:32,425
It's fine.

885
00:58:32,967 --> 00:58:35,011
You're welcome to visit us anytime.

886
00:58:36,888 --> 00:58:37,889
All of you.

887
00:58:38,890 --> 00:58:40,225
As well as Kazehaya.

888
00:58:44,812 --> 00:58:45,730
Thanks!

889
00:58:54,072 --> 00:58:54,906
Dad.

890
00:58:55,740 --> 00:58:59,577
You've been very understanding. Thank you.

891
00:59:02,664 --> 00:59:07,001
For New Year's...
you should go out again this year.

892
00:59:09,254 --> 00:59:11,381
You'll all be out past midnight, right?

893
00:59:11,464 --> 00:59:12,757
You better bundle up!

894
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:14,592
I don't need you catchin' a cold!

895
00:59:14,676 --> 00:59:16,261
Dad, hang on.

896
00:59:17,262 --> 00:59:19,389
I'm doing it because I want to.

897
00:59:21,057 --> 00:59:24,936
I thought it might be fun to do this...
that's why I chose it.

898
00:59:29,274 --> 00:59:31,943
My soba...

899
00:59:32,485 --> 00:59:36,990
...might not turn out very good this year,
but I'll give it my best shot!

900
01:00:05,018 --> 01:00:06,019
Hey, honey.

901
01:00:06,644 --> 01:00:07,478
Hmm?

902
01:00:10,565 --> 01:00:12,483
HAPPY BIRTHDAY
SAWAKO-CHAN

903
01:00:12,567 --> 01:00:15,486
Sawako looked
so happy today, didn't she?

904
01:00:15,570 --> 01:00:16,446
Yes.

905
01:00:17,196 --> 01:00:18,615
She did.

906
01:00:19,365 --> 01:00:22,493
She's definitely one
to speak her mind, don't you think?

907
01:00:23,077 --> 01:00:24,287
I'm glad.

908
01:00:24,370 --> 01:00:26,581
It must mean she feels safe to do so.

909
01:00:27,498 --> 01:00:29,876
Yeah. I think you're right.

910
01:00:30,793 --> 01:00:33,421
She's much more mature than I realized.

911
01:00:33,504 --> 01:00:36,466
To tell you the truth,
it just took me by surprise.

912
01:00:37,634 --> 01:00:38,760
Ten years, huh?

913
01:00:39,677 --> 01:00:41,554
Will it feel like forever?

914
01:00:41,638 --> 01:00:43,681
Or pass in the blink of an eye?

915
01:00:45,350 --> 01:00:47,935
If you think about it,
once graduation rolls around

916
01:00:48,019 --> 01:00:50,188
and she decides to move away for school...

917
01:00:51,356 --> 01:00:54,651
that leaves us all
with one more year of living together.

918
01:00:58,696 --> 01:00:59,781
I'm happy.

919
01:01:01,449 --> 01:01:05,912
So, so happy... to get to spend time

920
01:01:06,496 --> 01:01:10,166
with the people I love most in the world!

921
01:01:11,084 --> 01:01:14,128
I wish it could go on... forever.

922
01:01:14,879 --> 01:01:16,172
Just like this.
